Privacy Policy — UniMonk
Last updated: March 2026
UniMonk is developed and maintained by a single independent developer. This policy explains what data we collect, how we use it, and who we share it with.
What We Collect
We collect anonymous gameplay data such as session activity, game progress, and in-game behavior. If you create an account, we may also collect a username and any cosmetic preferences tied to that account. We do not collect your real name, email, or any personally identifiable information unless you choose to provide it.
How We Use Your Data
Data is used solely to provide and improve gameplay functionality, including multiplayer services, account management, and in-app purchases.
Third Party Services
UniMonk uses the following third party services which may process data on our behalf:

Photon (Exit Games) — multiplayer networking
Microsoft PlayFab — backend and account services
Meta Platform Services — VR platform integration and payments

Each of these services has their own privacy policy and data practices.
In-App Purchases
UniMonk offers optional in-app purchases including virtual currency, items, and a VIP room. All transactions are processed securely through Meta's native payment system. We do not store your payment information.
Data Sharing
We do not sell your data. We only share data with the third party services listed above as necessary to operate the game.
Children's Privacy
UniMonk is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children.
Your Rights
You may request deletion of your account and associated data at any time by contacting us.
Contact
If you have any questions about this policy, please reach out at Pavrbusiness@gmail.com
